  "askCmdr.consent.title": "Talk to Cmdr about your files",
  "@askCmdr.consent.title": {
    "sourceHash": "59b4ca9"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.intro": "Ask Cmdr sends your questions to the AI provider you choose, using your own API key. Here’s exactly what leaves your Mac when you chat:",
  "@askCmdr.consent.intro": {
    "sourceHash": "4366272"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.item.messages": "Your messages",
  "@askCmdr.consent.item.messages": {
    "sourceHash": "befc6e9"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.item.names": "The names and paths of files and folders Cmdr looks at to answer you",
  "@askCmdr.consent.item.names": {
    "sourceHash": "ce3259d"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.item.sizes": "Their sizes and dates",
  "@askCmdr.consent.item.sizes": {
    "sourceHash": "2484530"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.item.envelope": "What you’re looking at right now: your current folder, cursor, selection, and connected drives",
  "@askCmdr.consent.item.envelope": {
    "sourceHash": "2e5a0ef"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.item.attachments": "Any file or folder you attach to a question, by its name and path only",
  "@askCmdr.consent.item.attachments": {
    "sourceHash": "b9ad2af"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.item.memory": "The notes Ask Cmdr keeps about you, sent again with every message",
  "@askCmdr.consent.item.memory": {
    "sourceHash": "54bee04"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.noContents": "Cmdr doesn’t send the files themselves: no file contents, no photos, no thumbnails. Photo search is the one thing that reaches inside your images, and only when you have it search them: the text Cmdr recognized inside the matching photos and their tags go to your provider so it can find them. Ask Cmdr can suggest renames, moves, and cleanups, and nothing happens to a file until you approve it.",
  "@askCmdr.consent.noContents": {
    "sourceHash": "99f9add"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.memory": "Ask Cmdr writes itself notes about you: how you like things organized, what you’ve turned down before, anything you ask it to remember. Those notes ride along with every message you send, for as long as they exist, and they can include text Cmdr recognized inside your photos. You can read them, or wipe them, any time in the Ask Cmdr settings.",
  "@askCmdr.consent.memory": {
    "sourceHash": "80facfd"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.proactive": "Ask Cmdr also watches the folders you use and starts a conversation when it has something to suggest, so messages can reach your provider without you asking first. You can turn that off in the Ask Cmdr settings, under “On its own”.",
  "@askCmdr.consent.proactive": {
    "sourceHash": "1d0b671"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.local": "Your chats stay on your Mac, in a local database you can open and read. You pick the provider and model, and you can see what each conversation costs.",
  "@askCmdr.consent.local": {
    "sourceHash": "f7d4075"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.logsNote": "If you turn on LLM call logging in Advanced settings, Cmdr also saves each request and reply to a folder on your Mac. Those logs stay local too, never sent anywhere.",
  "@askCmdr.consent.logsNote": {
    "sourceHash": "7e211fc"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.accept": "Turn on Ask Cmdr",
  "@askCmdr.consent.accept": {
    "sourceHash": "0d656c4"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.decline": "Not now",
  "@askCmdr.consent.decline": {
    "sourceHash": "a0e63d7"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.whatsNew.title": "What’s changed since you turned this on",
  "@askCmdr.consent.whatsNew.title": {
    "sourceHash": "641705c"
  },
  "askCmdr.consent.whatsNew.body": "Ask Cmdr now keeps notes about you between chats, and it can start a conversation on its own when it notices something worth mentioning. That’s a bigger promise than the one you agreed to, so here it all is again.",
  "@askCmdr.consent.whatsNew.body": {
    "sourceHash": "88751a5"
  },
